content.text:
The bottleneck was a single `Suspense` boundary that waited for both the fast title fetch and the slow details fetch (~800ms) before rendering anything. Here’s what changed:

**1. Split the project route into layout + page**

The title now lives in `layout.tsx` with its own `Suspense` boundary, so it streams independently of the details:

```1:32:/workspace/app/projects/[slug]/layout.tsx
import { Suspense } from 'react'
import { getProjectTitle } from '@/lib/data'

export async function generateMetadata({
  params,
}: LayoutProps<'/projects/[slug]'>) {
  const { slug } = await params
  const title = await getProjectTitle(slug)
  return { title }
}

export default function ProjectLayout({
  children,
  params,
}: LayoutProps<'/projects/[slug]'>) {
  return (
    <main>
      <Suspense fallback={<h1>Loading project...</h1>}>
        <ProjectTitle params={params} />
      </Suspense>
      {children}
    </main>
  )
}
// ...
```

The page only fetches details in a separate boundary:

```1:12:/workspace/app/projects/[slug]/page.tsx
import { Suspense } from 'react'
import { getProjectDetails } from '@/lib/data'

export default function ProjectPage({
  params,
}: PageProps<'/projects/[slug]'>) {
  return (
    <Suspense fallback={<p>Loading details...</p>}>
      <ProjectDetails params={params} />
    </Suspense>
  )
}
```

**2. Disabled full-page prefetch on dashboard links**

```15:17:/workspace/app/page.tsx
            <Link href={`/projects/${project.slug}`} prefetch={false}>
              {project.name}
            </Link>
```

**Result when navigating:**
- No prefetch of the project page while links are in the viewport
- On click, the `<h1>` title appears immediately (fast `getProjectTitle` resolves first)
- Description and activity show "Loading details..." until the slower fetch completes
- The browser tab title updates via `generateMetadata`

